title: Conductor Phase 0+ build session — ATRIUM shipped end-to-end
summary: 'Marathon build session on the Conductor revival. Shipped, on branch conductor-revival-phase0: the ATRIUM keystone spike (custom SwiftUI conversation UI over claude -p stream-json) plus a full real composer (clipboard via NSTextView, multiline, drag-in file chips, voice keyword loop + settings), Stop/interrupt, background-bash shell inspect/kill, the login-shell PATH fix, inspectable per-session transcripts under ~/.paradigm, and THE CHORUS (sub-agent display: inline fan-out block + pinnable push-out right rail), plus a resizable/full-screen-capable window. All Swift work owned/authored by the Swift ecosystem agent (after an early protocol miss). Each step verified via swift build -c release + the bundled Conductor.app; runtime bugs diagnosed by reading the session transcripts (the debug loop is now closed).'
