learnings:
  - 'VERIFIED claude -p stream-json protocol (empirically): bidirectional turns via {type:user,message:{role:user,content:[{type:text,text}]}} on stdin (keep stdin open). INTERRUPT = {type:control_request,request_id,request:{subtype:interrupt}} → control_response success → result subtype error_during_execution (the bare {type:interrupt} is IGNORED). Background work emits system task_* events (task_started/task_progress/task_updated/task_notification).'
  - 'Sub-agent vs bash task events are self-attributing: task_started carries tool_use_id (links to the spawning Agent/Bash tool_use), task_type (local_agent vs local_bash), description, subagent_type, prompt; task_notification carries usage{total_tokens,tool_uses,duration_ms}. Type by task_type, correlate by tool_use_id — NEVER FIFO. Kill a background task via the TaskStop tool (NOT KillShell; that name is stale). Killed tasks report status failed/exit-144; completed report ''completed''. Background shell output is a readable file at the path in the tool_result (''Output is being written to: <path>.output'').'
  - 'macOS gotchas (Conductor is LSUIElement): (1) SwiftUI @main App owns the menu bar — add menu items via .commands, not AppKit NSMenu. (2) TCC mic prompt only fires from a real bundled .app (build-conductor.sh), never the bare .build/release binary. (3) A GUI/bundle-launched app has a minimal PATH — spawn child claude with a login-shell-captured env ($SHELL -lic env) or node/paradigm/hooks fail exit 127. (4) Clipboard + Enter/Shift+Enter need a native NSTextView (performKeyEquivalent + insertNewline), not a SwiftUI TextField in a manual NSWindow. (5) full-screen on accessory app needs collectionBehavior .fullScreenPrimary.'
  - 'Process meta-fix: ATRIUM logs every session''s full stream I/O to inspectable JSONL transcripts at ~/.paradigm/conductor/atrium/ + index.jsonl. This closed the debug loop — runtime bugs (stuck status, kill mislabel, sub-agents-as-shells) were diagnosed by READING the transcript instead of screenshots. Lesson: keep transcript logging non-lossy (an early lossy log misled a diagnosis).'
