body: |-
  Branch: conductor-revival-phase0 (commits 2c7732e0 → 175aa5d2; post-commit history h0453–h0469). Not merged; Matt publishes/merges himself.

  Shipped surfaces (all ATRIUM, Swift-owned): keystone stream round-trip; composer (NSTextView clipboard+multiline, file-drop chips, voice wake/send keyword loop "respond"/"send it" + Settings›Input keyword config, reusing WhisperKit/AudioCapture); Stop (control_request interrupt); background-bash shell panel (inspect = read .output file; kill = TaskStop; exit-reap on shutdown); login-shell PATH env; per-session transcripts; THE CHORUS (sub-agent inline fan-out block + pinnable push-out right rail, deterministic tool_use_id correlation + task_type typing + usage/duration); resizable/full-screen window (1100x780 default).

  Design language: "ATRIUM" (Mika) — calm dark cockpit; Atrium Amber reserved for human-attention; prose-over-mechanics; CHORUS = sub-agents as parallel voices (seed of a future FLEET view). Founder reframe: the REAL Conductor is a full-screen Claude-desktop-app experience; the floating spike is temporary.

  Open / v2: full nested sub-agent transcript drill-in (needs parent_tool_use_id on interleaved inner tool calls — absent so far); needs-human (amber) detection + retry; voice 'no words typed' still needs a live wake-word test or transcript check; interrupt-mid-Bash-tool live-confirm. Panel agentIds across the session are in the commit trail. Phase 1+ per the build plan (L-2026-06-15-215150-001).
